// Scripting: code in do blocks, processes and files, tasks, and funcs,
// macros and templates.
include = [
  "./code.heron",
  "./processes_and_files.heron.md",
  "./tasks.heron",
  "./funcs_and_templates.heron",
]

@lens(user, developer)
| The small executable [layer](#heron.language.specifications.layers.layer): what code in `do` blocks does, processes and files, tasks run by path, and funcs, macros and templates. It's kept small on purpose: code decides, combines and calls, real work runs in the language a system is built in, and what stays is deterministic, so every run is replayable.

tasks_in_tree: goal(measure = "Build, test and release run from the tree.") {{
  Teams run their build, test and release tasks from the same tree that specifies them, with a record of every run.
}}
